| 4     | Risk Gates + Breaker    | 20 min   | Leverage/size/loss gates + circuit breaker |
| 5     | Thinking Loop           | 20 min   | ReAct loop with tool calling             |
| 6     | Wiring                  | 15 min   | AgentEngine class                        |
| 7     | Memory Distillation     | 15 min   | Periodic summarization (optional)        |
| **Total** |                         | **~3 hrs** |                                          |

---

## What Makes This Architecture Scalable

### 1. Provider Abstraction
- Swap ASI:One ↔ Heurist ↔ OpenAI without changing agent code
- Model router picks best model per task complexity
- Easy to add new providers later

### 2. Tool System
- Add new tools by creating a file + calling `registry.register()`
- Tools are self-describing (JSON schema)
- AI can discover and use tools automatically

### 3. Memory System
- Episodic (raw trades) + Semantic (embeddings) + Distilled (patterns)
- Vector search for "similar situations"
- Periodic distillation keeps memory clean

### 4. Decision Pipeline
- Thinking → Risk Gates → Circuit Breaker → Execute
- Each layer is independent and testable
- Easy to add new risk rules

### 5. Observability
- Every decision has full reasoning trace
- WebSocket broadcasts for real-time monitoring
- Feed events for audit trail

